    <node id="Registry Entry">
      <data key="d0">Registry Entry</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">**Registry Entry**

A registry entry is a formal record stored within a registry system that documents a stated relationship between two identifiers, such as a subregion and a larger region or other related entities. The entry captures the nature of the relationship and includes a source assertion that indicates the provenance or reference supporting the claim. By recording both the relationship and its source, the registry entry provides a verifiable link between the entities involved and the evidence that establishes the connection. This documentation is essential for maintaining accurate, traceable, and authoritative information within the registry, ensuring that users can assess the validity and context of the asserted relationships. In the context of a fictional reference world, a registry entry records information about subregions and their relationships to larger regions, describing the connections between identifiers while noting the source assertion without evaluating other registry entries. The entry serves as a generic record that holds information about a registry item, its relationships, and the supporting evidence. It may also contain information about another registry entry, thereby linking related records within the system.&lt;SEP&gt;A record in a registry that stores information about other entries.</data>
      <data key="d3">D0b3092068b267ade7047-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D1759848a15f03afde86d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D1e6fcd119ed03eaa5770-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D213d059cbf8275626d71-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D307f61e2bb61c65dbffa-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D31d7efaecc9dac0459f5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D32fee42740fc2d3298a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D3987590ecfb6040326d8-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D3bf755801edbd55b30c7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D47c49cfab181f97b6a71-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D484ceaf31f69109851b6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D4ff1724729c0dc75dac1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D51c37d21d0db8f1e9c74-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D69ab7fa586361d0bba4c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D6ae5922c2a4aebab2026-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D6d1b7dca231782eb5c7f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D76413fefe6657c0277f5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D813a5727276cc4bd97d1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D8c8029e8c48a14776585-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D8e1819f9a41f64977ff5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D9a3ed82160e45022573d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Da175516fb4d2dd15b1c8-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Dacb8c3df2f00f4b6989f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Db8ef2d8f24e3cb70b9e7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Dbafebf997bd9cd9d8308-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Dbb866ffea43863d04da8-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Dc3ec77827ceea4dcff0a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Dd1555d1f4e34553d103d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Dd1b71a1b0a096adfd662-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Dd9fb9c37159b590d129d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Ddd90b4110e833cad50f5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Ddf4508c438a35f9493ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;De251762bf8dc191c5046-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;De3f35bb5cd2daf23678e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;De5d52bc41134b6f51dcf-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;De791e97b2b1adf07df4f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Deb75e238ae54da5ebf3e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Df08f83e6fbc691cf3e31-chunk-000</data>
